<body>

<!-- ══════════ HEADER ══════════ -->
<header class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="badge">Trend Analysis Report</div>
    <h1>BIEK Computer Science 12th Class<br>Past Paper Analysis (2015–2025)</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive examination of 11 years of HSC Part-2 question patterns, type distributions, and topic evolution — designed to guide curriculum planning and exam preparation strategy.</p>
    <div class="meta">
      <div class="meta-item"><span class="label">Dataset</span><span class="value">327 Questions</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><span class="label">Years Covered</span><span class="value">2015 – 2025</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><span class="label">Examination</span><span class="value">BIEK HSC Part-2</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><span class="label">Subject</span><span class="value">Computer Science</span></div>
      <div class="meta-item"><span class="label">Audience</span><span class="value">Educators &amp; Curriculum Planners</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ══════════ MAIN ══════════ -->
<main>
<div class="container">

  <!-- ── SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ── -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">1</div>
      <h2>Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <div class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
          <div class="kpi-label">Total Questions</div>
          <div class="kpi-value">327</div>
          <div class="kpi-sub">Across 10 exam years</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card accent">
          <div class="kpi-label">MCQ Questions</div>
          <div class="kpi-value">150</div>
          <div class="kpi-sub">45.9% of total</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card green">
          <div class="kpi-label">Short Questions</div>
          <div class="kpi-value">147</div>
          <div class="kpi-sub">44.9% of total</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card red">
          <div class="kpi-label">Long Questions</div>
          <div class="kpi-value">30</div>
          <div class="kpi-sub">9.2% of total</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card">
          <div class="kpi-label">Avg Questions/Year</div>
          <div class="kpi-value">32.7</div>
          <div class="kpi-sub">Range: 27 – 36</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card">
          <div class="kpi-label">Years Represented</div>
          <div class="kpi-value">10</div>
          <div class="kpi-sub">2015–2025, excl. 2020</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>This analysis draws on a community-compiled question bank of <strong>327 BIEK Computer Science HSC Part-2 questions</strong> spanning ten examination years from 2015 to 2025. Each question is categorised into one of three types: <span class="pill pill-mcq">MCQs</span>, <span class="pill pill-short">Short</span>, or <span class="pill pill-long">Long</span>. The dataset covers the theory portion of Paper-II; practical components are excluded.</p>

      <div class="missing-note">
        ⚠ <strong>Data Gap:</strong> No questions from 2020 are present in this dataset. The year 2020 is entirely absent — likely due to the COVID-19 pandemic affecting examination schedules or paper availability. All analyses skip from 2019 directly to 2021.
      </div>

      <h3>Question Type Breakdown</h3>
      <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <div>
          <div class="chart-title">Overall Type Distribution</div>
          <div class="chart-container" style="height:220px;">
            <canvas id="donutChart"></canvas>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>The BIEK Computer Science exam has maintained a <strong>balanced two-way split</strong> between objective and subjective assessment throughout the study period. MCQs and Short Questions each represent roughly <strong>45% of all questions</strong>, while Long Questions constitute just over <strong>9%</strong>.</p>
          <p>Despite this small proportional share, Long Questions carry significant weight in actual marking schemes, as each typically contains multiple sub-parts (a), (b), and (c) covering distinct topics simultaneously.</p>
          <p>Every year without exception includes exactly <strong>15 MCQs and 3 Long Questions</strong>. The only variable component is the Short Questions section, which changed across three distinct phases (explained in Section 3).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── SECTION 2: YEARLY DISTRIBUTION ── -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-number">2</div>
      <h2>Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">

      <div class="chart-title">Total Questions Per Year (2015–2025)</div>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:280px; margin-bottom:28px;">
        <canvas id="lineChart"></canvas>
      </div>

      <div class="insight-box">
        <strong>Key Finding:</strong> The exam underwent a significant structural expansion in <strong>2017</strong>, increasing total questions by 33% (from 27 to 36) — exclusively through the addition of Short Questions (from 9 to 18). This format was held for three years (2017–2019) before reverting to 33 questions per year from 2021 onward, establishing the current stable format.
      </div>

      <h3>Detailed Year-by-Year Data</h3>
      <table class="data-table">
